","n":1},{"id":77376330613218,"type":"genre","name":"Stoner Metal","n":1},{"id":64491050809040,"type":"genre","name":"Doom Metal","n":1}],"labels":[{"id":248498756812798,"type":"label","name":"Roadrunner Records","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":19,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"}],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[],"book_tracks":[],"mentions":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Subsidized by Nickelback Profits","body":"Mastodon, a metal band, benefited from the profits Nickelback generated for Roadrunner Records. The substantial sales from Nickelback helped subsidize the releases of various other metal bands, showcasing their role in financially sustaining parts of the music industry. \"When Nickelback was selling millions for roadrunner records, that money subsidized releases for a ton of metal bands like Opef and Kill Switch Engage and Mastodon.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"10 Things That Really Annoy Me","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Zniri9uSlc"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Impact on Music Industry Ecosystem","body":"Despite widespread criticism and \"irrational global hatred,\" Nickelback is recognized as a vital component of the music industry's ecosystem. Their commercial success and high album sales meant they were a \"hit band\" that generated substantial profits. This revenue, particularly during their tenure with Roadrunner Records, was instrumental in subsidizing releases for numerous metal bands such as Opeth, Killswitch Engage, and Mastodon, and also provided crucial \"seed money\" for Billy Talent's entry into the US market. They exemplify the \"rule of 30\" in music, where a few highly successful acts financially support many others. \"They are an important part of the music industry ecosystem.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Nickelback","from_id":8924700468938,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"10 Things That Really Annoy Me","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Zniri9uSlc"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Subsidized by Nickelback Profits","body":"Opeth, a metal band, was among those whose releases were financially supported by the significant profits generated by Nickelback's album sales for Roadrunner Records. This highlights Nickelback's role within the music industry's ecosystem, where hit bands subsidize other acts. \"When Nickelback was selling millions for roadrunner records, that money subsidized releases for a ton of metal bands like Opef and Kill Switch Engage and Mastodon.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Opeth","from_id":18586207499585,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"10 Things That Really Annoy Me","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Zniri9uSlc"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Subsidized by Nickelback Profits","body":"Killswitch Engage, a metal band, was one of the acts whose releases were subsidized by the millions in sales Nickelback generated for Roadrunner Records. This demonstrates the financial interdependence within the music industry, where successful bands help fund the development and releases of other artists. \"When Nickelback was selling millions for roadrunner records, that money subsidized releases for a ton of metal bands like Opef and Kill Switch Engage and Mastodon.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Killswitch Engage","from_id":150835240019815,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"10 Things That Really Annoy Me","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Zniri9uSlc"}]}],"charts":[{"id":235637470503624,"type":"album","name":"Remission","work_year":2002,"list_id":44735175437010,"list":"AOTY Must Hear 2000s","src":"charts","rank":410,"year":2002,"note":null,"yt":"39j-jvK9Mx4","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":235637470503624,"type":"album","name":"Remission","list_id":79201857171461,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Hardcore [Punk]","src":"musthear","ran